@meta
id: 20-08
title: The black hole
chapter: 20
type: lesson
skills: register-blackhole
par: 34
minutes: 5
vscode: copy, then delete with the Delete key so the clipboard survives
open: order.provider.ts

@brief
Sometimes a delete is just a delete. You do not want the text back, you
do not want it in your history, and above all you do not want it to
overwrite the thing you were about to put. For that there is a register
that swallows whatever goes in: the black hole, `"_`. `"_dd` removes the
line and leaves every other register exactly as it was.

`settle` has a placeholder comment where its status guard should be.
The guard is the three-line `if` block in `cancel`. Replace the comment
line with a copy of the block, using a plain `p` or `P` for the put —
not `"0`. Make the delete get out of the way instead.

@keys
| `"_dd` | delete the line into nothing |
| `"_d{motion}` | any delete, into nothing |
| `P` | put before — and it still holds the yank |

@hints
Yank the guard first. Then delete the comment in a way that does not
touch the unnamed register, and the plain put still holds the guard.
--
`"_dd` on the comment line leaves you on the line after it. `P` puts the
guard above that, which is where the comment was.
--
`/if (order` Enter, `3yy`, `/TODO` Enter, `"_dd`, `P`.

@solution
    /if (order<Enter> 3yy  /TODO<Enter> "_dd P  :wq<Enter>

You met `"0p` in the first lesson and it would have worked here too, so
it is fair to ask why the black hole exists. Two reasons.

The first is that a black-hole delete changes nothing about what
`p` will do next. Whatever habit you have built around `p`, `P` and `.`
keeps working, because the thing you did not want never entered the
register at all.

The second shows up in lesson 20-10: every delete also gets shifted into
a numbered history, `"1` through `"9`. Deleting junk pushes the thing
you actually want one slot further down. `"_` keeps the history clean.

Say it to yourself as "delete into nothing". The underscore is the
floor of the register box; things dropped there do not come back.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async settle(id: string, total: number) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    // TODO: same guard as cancel

    await this.paymentService.capture(order.id, total);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'SETTLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async settle(id: string, total: number) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.capture(order.id, total);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'SETTLED' },
    });
  }
}
